Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"5ffb811b-8b32-e24e-85d1-2034478c82c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"780e8777-c25a-964b-8f4f-5f0fd4a63d04"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"222d9937-f5e7-6c4b-8c13-7a2a0aee570b"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"e984251b-a8ce-da40-b3e2-afd6d683389c"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9631782d-9f70-8541-82bf-bb163660eb79"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e34170f3-b2ba-de48-ac6b-92d8438f5bb7"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"1cd5e472-fc99-184d-9f03-03b8c6350b27"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fd68f271-e5b9-e846-b3ef-9430321fca84"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2ab51933-cec6-8f4c-891b-b629a32c09a2"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9a72d107-d90f-2a4d-9562-41db3b296171"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e3ac9b99-5a28-2746-a470-493fc53ace0c"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"3b7ff8d6-18ea-714d-b9a7-e3ab2b2b3c15"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"2237ef0a-c0ac-8d44-8f33-463a6ac6b989"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c331fd60-3cb0-9d45-8c77-711e7c0ea207"],

